  title="How to map the literature on a topic: citation graphs explained"
  description="Map a research field with citation graphs: backward and forward citations, co-citation, bibliographic coupling and similar papers, plus tools that draw the map."
  question="How do you map the literature on a research topic?"
  answer="Start from a few papers you know are central, then follow their citations both ways: the older papers they cite and the newer papers citing them. Papers that are often cited together (co-citation) or that cite the same sources (bibliographic coupling) belong to the same conversation. A citation graph draws this as a network, where clusters show sub-topics and heavily linked papers show the foundations."
  updated="2026-09-25"
